// phdl-introspection-attributes (PIA-04) — the device-introspection metadata
// attribute schemas, textually declared so ctrl+click on `@model`/`@name`/
// `@unit`/`@description`/`@kind` resolves to a real declaration (MD-24) and
// the names exist as first-class schema entries in every compilation unit's
// `SchemaRegistry` (the LSP's `SymbolKind::AttrSchema` arm reads the
// `decl_span` `register.rs` threads through from this header).
//
// Per MD-26 these are small, single-purpose, composable attributes — not
// role-shaped bundles (`@opvar`/`@observable`/`@terminal`). Model identity is
// the one deliberate pair: `@model(type, version)` carries both fields (a
// model type is meaningless without its version). The atomic `@kind` is
// placement-resolved: on a `var` it names an `ObservableKind`, on a port/wire
// a `TerminalKind` (the resolver in `pom/design.rs::introspection_meta` picks
// the target enum by POM node type).
//
// The PHDL attribute-argument grammar is keyed-only (`parse_attributes` in
// `parse/parser/attributes.rs` parses `ident = expr` pairs), so each
// single-field schema declares its value under a `value: String` field and
// authors write e.g. `@name(value = "i_d")` (user decision 2026-07-23). Every
// attribute is optional — omission yields the codegen-derived default, never
// an error (zero regression on existing stdlib models).
//
// Embedded unconditionally into every project's prelude (`resolve.rs`
// `prelude_items`, alongside `types`/`math`/`tasks`/`operators`) — unlike
// `device_port.phdl` (plugin-gated), introspection metadata is a stdlib
// concern every project needs. Loaded after `types.phdl` because the field
// types reference the primitive `String`.
extern attribute model {
    type: String,
    version: String,
}
extern attribute name {
    value: String,
}
extern attribute unit {
    value: String,
}
extern attribute description {
    value: String,
}
extern attribute kind {
    value: String,
}
